Vector is also called as legacy collection because it is replaced by more efficient collection which is ArrayList.
Vector works similar to ArrayList. Its underlined data structure is Resizable/Growable Array.
The differnece between Vector and ArrayList is that The initial capacity of the Vector is 10 which is similar in ArrayList as well but,
the incremental capacity once the vector is full equals to 2x of the current capacity means double while in ArrayList it is determined by
(current capacity * 3/2) + 1

The second important difference between these two is the Vector is Thread safe (Synchronized) which means only a single thread can use it to
access the data while the ArrayList is Not Thread safe(Not-Synchronized) which means a number of threads can use it to access the data within it,
which makes ArrayList more efficient because more operaetions can be performed and data can be accessed quickly.

Another difference is that the Vector has 4 contructors while ArrayList has 3 constructors.
